Fixes #349046

**Stacked on #349078** (`compactAllowsSplit`); this PR's base is that branch, so the diff shows only this change. Retarget to `main` once #349078 has merged.

`workbench.action.newChatWindow` now accepts options, like `workbench.action.chat.open`:

```ts
interface INewChatWindowOptions {
	/** The agent the new chat starts with: a mode kind or a custom agent's name (as in workbench.action.chat.open). */
	readonly mode?: string;
	/** Text to put into the chat input, without sending it. */
	readonly query?: string;
	/** Options of the new window (compact, compactAllowsSplit, bounds, alwaysOnTop), merged over the defaults (compact, 640x640). */
	readonly auxiliary?: IEditorOptions['auxiliary'];
}

vscode.commands.executeCommand('workbench.action.newChatWindow', { mode: 'Agent Fix', auxiliary: { compactAllowsSplit: true } });
```

`query` is applied right away. Custom agents may still be loading in a new window, so the command waits up to 5 s for the agent to appear; otherwise the chat keeps the default agent. Without options, the command behaves as before.

Used by Team Tools' Agent Fix (microsoft/vscode-packages#453), which opens its report beside the chat.

**Validation:** core typecheck. Tested manually in Code OSS with Team Tools: its bug button opens a compact chat window with the Agent Fix agent, and with `compactAllowsSplit` the report opens beside the chat while the window stays compact.
